      "card_ids": ["C86","C87","C88","C89","C90","C91","C92","C93","C94","C95","C96","C97"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability experiment is available; L6 records are for reference molecules, mostly mephenytoin CYP2C19 variants and unrelated microsome controls.",
    "The closest L6 analog (compound 28) differs from the query in scaffold and chloro substitution; its human/mouse hepatocyte CLint values are not directly transferable.",
    "L4/L5 records are analog absorption/permeability evidence, not query-specific F measurements; repeated records are not independent votes.",
    "First-pass hepatic extraction for the query is not quantified; moderate intrinsic clearance alone would not imply F<20% given favorable absorption."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds no affirmative F<20% evidence: most hepatic-clearance records are for mephenytoin variants or unrelated controls, and the only structurally related hepatocyte CLint record (compound 28) is not a direct bioavailability outcome and does not outweigh the consistent favorable absorption/permeability and related high-F context. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

